mark we were talking a little earlier  about the way that sport is severing  ties with russia and confirmation in the  last few minutes from fifa the world  governing body of football and also uefa  who run the game in europe that they are  suspending all russian teams from  international competitions which is a  step that has been called for for a  couple of days now and nations have been  lining up to say that they would refuse  to play in any level against a russian  team and fifa have now finally taken the  decision they've said in a statement  fifa and uefa have today decided  together that all russian teams whether  national representative teams or club  teams shall be suspended from  participation in both fifa and uefa  competitions until further notice so  that will mean  that russia  are  very unlikely to take part in the  playoffs for the world cup for the men's  world cup that are due to be scheduled  for next month they're due to play  poland in that series of playoff games  that will not happen perhaps there will  be a replacement team the women's euro  competition is taking place in england  this summer the final here at wembley  russia very unlikely to be part of that  and spartak moscow are a club side who  are in the europa league competition in  europe they will be unable to take part  given the news of that ban that  uefa and fifa have put in place today on  a day in which the olympics have also  encouraged  sporting organizers and competitions to  ban russian and belarusian athletes a  very significant day yet again in the  world of sport as organizations and  governing bodies sever their ties with  vladimir putin's russia and there are no  exceptions this time it is a clear  suspension from fifa and uefa which  means russian involvement in coming  sporting tournaments both from club  level and also on international level  well those russian sides will not be  allowed to take part
 

